{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on S3 2.4(a), answering 7a73e352: choice (i). A valid GitHub root must be one of the installed registers: the pin, or a root that INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES lists; otherwise the configuration is misconfigured, creation refuses and /health answers 503. I checked the live roots (secret names through the account API, 09:25 EST): none of the account's ten Workers holds GITHUB_APP_CONFIG as a secret, no committed Wrangler config sets it, and /health on dap-grow, dap-lending and dap-demo reports wiring.github off, reason unconfigured. So (i) refuses no deployed Worker. Every room Worker also sets DEPLOYMENT: grow, commons and connect as config vars; lending, demo and artroom-scope as secrets. Keep the health.test.ts:138 case, rewritten to expect misconfigured, plus one case where INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES lists the older root and creation proceeds. Name the operator step (list an older GitHub root in INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES before deploying) in docs/deploy.md.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}